Rallied monkeys charge death resolved against Kumbhakarṇa --- Kumbhakarṇa scatters thousands and devours monkeys like Garuḍa snakes --- Hanumān rains peaks and trees and is pierced by spear --- Nīla with R̥ṣabha Śarabha Gavākṣa Gandhamādana falls bloodied --- Swarming monkeys bite climb as Kumbhakarṇa devours them survivors flee to Rāma --- Sugrīva hurls mountain and is felled then seized toward Laṅkā --- Hanumān steadies host while Sugrīva bites ears and nose and escapes --- Kumbhakarṇa starved devours friends and foes alike --- Lakṣmaṇa plants shafts then Rāma plants Raudra shafts --- Rāma lops both arms severs feet fills mouth with shafts --- Rāma severs mountainlike head as Indra severed Vr̥tra gods monkeys praise earth trembles